WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.820
Tesla has registered 158 cybercabs in Texas, more than doubling the fleet in under two weeks. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 623. Ming posted on X that Optimus could have the best debut on Halloween Day. The post appeared at 8.21 in the morning on October 2nd, and drew 25 views. The timing lines up with seasonal interest in robotics demonstrations. Observers have tracked similar social media speculation ahead of prior hardware reveals.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:36.380
MING also stated that AI5 is Tesla's next big thing right now, since the age of the Model

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:36.740
3.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:41.780
That post came at 816 the same morning and received 35 views.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:47.420
The comparison places the upcoming silicon alongside the vehicle that first scaled Tesla's

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.140
volume production.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:53.640
Community discussion has centered on how the chip supports both vehicle and robot workloads.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:59.800
MING further noted that in semiconductor manufacturing, drafting off established industry scale

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.720
Beats custom cut-downs every single time.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:07.600
The approach protects unit costs and delivery schedules when scaling into the millions.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.920
The post arrived at 813 and received 34 views.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:17.400
The comment addresses trade-offs between custom silicon and off-the-shelf memory components.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:23.120
Tesla's new driveway feature lets drivers shift into drive and pull away while the charging

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:24.380
cable remains connected.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:34.020
Vehicles need software version 2026.38.3 or later. Pre-2021 Model S and X vehicles are not supported.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:43.800
The feature applies to U.S. supercharges only for now. Tesla described the function as intended strictly for emergencies and warned that misuse will trigger penalties.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:52.140
Electric Vehicle Council data shows Tesla and Polestar delivered 5,854 EVs in September, 2026.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:02:02.760
Tesla delivered 5,654 vehicles up 21.3% year-on-year. The Model Y represented roughly 76% of the combined

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:11.120
Tesla and Polestar volume for the month. The Model 3 recorded 1178 sales up 60% on the same period

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:19.300
last year. Tesla has now registered 158 cybercabs in Texas. The fleet grew from 69 registered units on

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.840
on September 23 to 158 by October 2.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:25.920
The latest batch added 32 vehicles.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:29.720
Elon Musk said Tesla cut the AI-5 chips memory

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.600
in half to 72 gigabytes.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:36.820
The AI-6 chips memory was cut by a third to 144 gigabytes.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.440
Musk called the cuts the only way

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.620
to get enough volume for optimist production.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.440
The changes should have a negligible effect

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:47.100
on optimist performance because memory bandwidth

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.920
with is the larger limiting factor.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.080
Tesla posted a short teaser clip on X

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.020
with the caption Halloween is coming.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.680
The clip previews a spooky transformation

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.240
coming to the center touchscreen.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:00.880
The post continues Tesla's pattern

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.160
of seasonal software updates that alter vehicle interfaces.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.800
Tesla has begun rolling out dynamic headlight leveling

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:08.860
to select vehicles.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.180
Owners reported the feature appearing

00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:12.640
without an official announcement.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.840
The update adjusts headlight aim automatically

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:21.740
based on vehicle load and road conditions. Tesla continues development of wireless charging hardware

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:27.720
for vehicles. A patent application details detection of foreign objects on the pad via resident

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:34.040
frequency changes. The system aims to improve safety during inductive charging sessions. Tesla

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:41.160
opened 2,700 supercharger stalls in the third quarter. That represents a 15% increase year over year.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:46.360
The network delivered 2.4 terawatt hours across 69 million sessions.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:51.320
The expansion continues the company's focus on growing charging infrastructure alongside

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.320
vehicle sales.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:57.320
Owners notice the CyberCab blows air on the B pillar camera at stoplights.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.840
The feature activates when there is no headwind to clear the lens.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.760
Owners ask whether other Tesla models use the same system.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:10.320
The observation highlights ongoing refinements to the purpose built Robotaxi's sensor suite.

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:15.460
Nissan acknowledged it can improve its electric SUV that competes with the model Y.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:19.120
The company is evaluating additional new electric vehicles.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.440
Sales of the current rival remain below expectations.

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:27.760
Nissan executives stated the existing product has not met internal volume targets.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:33.080
Cybertruck owners are triggering higher toll rights on the Pell Bridge due to vehicle weight.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:36.840
The bridge authority confirmed the heavier classification applies.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:42.080
owners pay the increased rate on each crossing. The classification reflects the

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.720
Cybertruck's curb weight compared with lighter passenger vehicles. An oil-

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:50.280
supply disruption could improve the total cost of ownership case for the

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:55.220
Tesla semi. Fleets facing higher diesel prices would see faster payback on

00:04:55.220 --> 00:05:00.320
electric trucks. The article examines route economics under elevated fuel costs.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:05.060
Higher diesel prices narrow the gap between upfront vehicle cost and lifetime

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:11.260
time operating savings. Multiple operators are expanding Robotaxi services in Austin alongside

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:17.280
Tesla's CyberCab fleet. The video tracks regulatory filings and vehicle registrations in the city.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:23.620
Tesla's unsupervised operations remain the largest by registered units. Competing services

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:29.200
continue to add vehicles while awaiting further regulatory clarity. Tesla shares are on track

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:34.320
for their worst week in two months ahead of third-quarter delivery figures. Analysts note

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:38.180
that any miss on volume expectations could extend the recent pullback.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:43.660
The company has not yet released the official delivery tally. Memory capacity and memory

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:48.420
bandwidth trade off differently once a system moves from training to inference at the edge.

00:05:49.020 --> 00:05:55.080
Cutting total memory on the AI5 and AI6 chips lowers die size and therefore cost per unit.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:06:00.180
Yet the bandwidth available to the neural network remains the binding constraint for real-time

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:05.480
control loops in a humoid. That distinction explains why the performance impact can stay

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:10.940
small even after having or trimming the memory footprint. The same arithmetic appears

00:06:10.940 --> 00:06:15.960
in other high-volume robotics programs. When the limiting factor is how many weights can

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:21.180
be moved per inference cycle, rather than how many weights can be stored, designers accept

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:26.320
smaller on-chip SRAM in exchange for cheaper fabrication and higher production volume.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:29.520
Tesla's decision follows that pattern exactly.

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:35.000
For Optimus, the cost reduction matters more than marginal accuracy gains, because the

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:39.600
robot must reach price points that compete with human labor across thousands of tasks.

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:45.020
Lower memory specifications accelerate that cost curve, without changing the fundamental

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.120
bandwidth-limited performance envelope.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:52.500
Before we go, the next batch of cyber-cab registrations in Texas will show whether the

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.980
rapid fleet growth continues.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:57.120
And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

